 "conclusion": "For n = 1,2,3 and every gb in C^{4n}: gamma_gb = delta f_gb + lambda_gb([.,.]_0)*1 with the explicit odd map f_gb : g -> g and the odd functional lambda_gb (= -gb/2 on odd generators).  Modulo scalars (adjoint representation) gamma_gb is therefore a coboundary for ALL gb; f_gb is unique up to inner odd derivations ad_Z, Z in g_1.  The scalar residual vanishes iff gb = 0, so exact equality in U(A) with f confined to g holds only for gb = 0."
